 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Board of width columns and height rows; rectangles are inclusive cell boxes given by top-left (x1,y1) and bottom-right (x2,y2) with x1<=x2, y1<=y2 inside the board. addRectangle returns the next positive id starting at 1 (ids never reused) and places it on top. getTopRectangle(x,y) returns the id of the topmost active rectangle covering the cell, or -1 if none. Levels 2-3 add removeRectangle and bringToFront. Level 4 (STACK tag) adds undo(): reverts the most recent not-yet-undone successful add/remove/bringToFront exactly (undoing an add deactivates that id without freeing it; undoing a remove restores its previous stacking position; undoing bringToFront restores the previous order) and returns true, or false if nothing remains. Failed calls are not recorded.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
